{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For the leader, for the sons of Korah</b> — This psalm is for the days of the Messiah. And Rabbi Moses said: it was said concerning Babylon. And some say: it was in the days of David when they brought up the Ark, and the proof is \"Elohim has gone up with a teru'ah,\" but this is not correct, because of \"He chooses for us our inheritance,\" and the one who explained this answered that this is a hint to Mount Moriah, for we cannot know when this psalm was said."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {0 "Resolved 'Rabbi Moses' as Ibn Ezra's standard reference to Rabbi Moses ha-Kohen Ibn Gikatilla; the phrase 'and the one who explained this answered' appears to introduce a defender of the Ark interpretation responding to the objection."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:06.493205628Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}